# AXIS SIBLING (Track K, Dict-storage cell) -- Dict subscript of a
# `Callable[void(int &)]` value writes through to the caller's `int` slot,
# exactly as calling `bump(&a)` directly does.
#
# AXIS / CELL:
#   Dict-of-Callable storage x plain-local int root x `&`-arg spelling.
# Complement of `callable_amp_arr_indexed_callee.gg` (Vector storage); the
# discriminator between them is the collection SHAPE (Vector[C] vs. Dict[K, C]).
#
# Pre-Track-K (measured at gorget-1 tip `1ec3ba55`): `gg check` clean, `gg
# build` clean, binary exits 139 (SIGSEGV) on BOTH C and LLVM -- identical
# failure mode to the Vector sibling because
# `infer_collection_element_type`'s Dict arm at
# `src/ir/lowering/exprs/methods.rs` had the SAME empty-params FnPtr writer
# gap (fixed in the same file in Track K).
void bump(int &n):
    n = n + 100

void main():
    int a = 1
    Dict[String, Callable[void(int &)]] d = {}
    d.put("f", bump)
    d["f"](&a)
    print(a)
